# AGENTS.md — Backend (PetsApp)

Entry point for backend work. Prefer ports and adapters: services depend on
repository ports (`Symbol` tokens), never on Drizzle types directly.

## Stack

- **NestJS 12** + TypeScript (ESM, `"type": "module"`)
- **Drizzle ORM** on **PostgreSQL** (`pg`); database specs use isolated real PostgreSQL via **TEST_DATABASE_URL**
- Auth: JWT in body + HttpOnly session cookie (`petsapp_session` /
  `__Host-petsapp_session`), CSRF Origin checks, roles
  `admin` | `super_admin` | `member`
- DTOs with `class-validator` + global validation
- Tests: **Vitest** (unit + in-process e2e); lint: **oxlint** (`npm run lint`)

## Skill routing

| Task | Skill / doc |
| --- | --- |
| Modules, controllers, guards, DI | `.cursor/skills/nestjs/SKILL.md` when present; otherwise match existing `src/**` modules |
| Persistence, migrations, repositories | `.cursor/skills/drizzle-orm/SKILL.md` when present; see `src/db/`, `src/**/infrastructure/` |
| Auth, roles, DTOs, OWASP | `.cursor/skills/backend-security-rules/SKILL.md` / `owasp-top10` when present |
| Logging | `Logger` from `@nestjs/common` or `src/logging/`; never log passwords, tokens, or full bodies |
| Tests | Vitest configs in `backend/`; use isolated PostgreSQL for database specs; retain in-memory repository fakes for pure unit contracts |

## Base rules

- Controllers stay thin: DTO + guards + service call.
- Map expected business failures to the right HTTP status; do not return 500
  for known domain errors.
- Every `@Injectable()` service that mutates state should log success/rejection
  without secrets.
- Seed the first `super_admin` with `npm run seed:admin` (see `backend/README.md`).

